+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+Tool input is checked against the registered JSON Schema at the registry boundary so a malformed model call becomes a correctable tool result.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming a missing required property before calling the executor; valid input, including undeclared extra properties, reaches the executor unchanged, while an unknown tool name still throws ([validated by: returns a required-field result before execution and passes valid extra keys through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14)).
+- A wrong-typed property is rejected with its path and expected type, without including its value in the returned result or logs ([validated by: rejects a wrong type with the property path and constraint but without the identifying value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L32)).
+- A static tool schema is compiled at registration, so an invalid schema throws then with the tool name; the compiled validator is reused across calls ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static schema at registration with the tool name](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L47)).
+- A function-valued definition is resolved on each execution, and validation follows the schema object returned for that call, with validators cached by schema object ([validated by: uses the current schema from a function-valued definition on each call](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L57)).
+- The orchestrator returns a rejected call as a tool result to the provider, which can retry a corrected call within the configured tool-round bound ([validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the provider so it can retry within the tool loop](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L77)).
+
+## Constraints
+
+Validation enforces required properties, declared types, and enums from the registered schema. It does not add an `additionalProperties: false` rule, coerce input, apply defaults, or provide an opt-out flag. Rejection messages and log lines contain failing property paths and constraints, never property values.
